B. Test Rig Interference
This section presents comparison of thrust measurements between the first and second phases of testing to assess the test rig interference effects on rear propeller performance. Figure 13 shows a comparison of CTISO and CTRear ISO for J = 0.47, J = 0.58, and J = 0.67. The bars for CTISO represent the maximum and minimum values between three repeat runs. The bars for CTRear ISO represent the maximum and minimum measurements for four runs in which the rear propeller assembly was placed at different locations along the horizontal rail at separation distances ranging from d = 2.1R to d = 4.7R relative to the front propeller assembly. There is good agreement between CTISO and CTRear ISO for αε[-60°,-10°]. This suggests that there are negligible test rig interference effects on the rear propeller performance in this angle of attack range, likely because the rear propeller disk is positioned well above the front fairing wake. Interference effects appear to be present in the angle of attack range of αε[-10°,40°], indicated by the decrease in CTRear ISO relative to CTISO. The thrust coefficients converge for the advance ratio cases of J = 0.58 and J = 0.67 at approximately α = 35°. The percent difference between CTISO and CTRear ISO is shown in Fig. 13(d) and is below 6.5% for all conditions presented. A comparison at J = 0.33 is not presented because the combination of rotor speed and freestream velocity were different between the isolated and tandem configuration datasets.
